WEBVTT

00:03.880 --> 00:04.560
All right guys.

00:04.560 --> 00:06.720
So now let's have a quick summary about tables.

00:06.760 --> 00:11.680
Tables in database are like spreadsheet or grid that contains columns and rows.

00:11.720 --> 00:14.640
And your actual data are stored in these tables.

00:14.640 --> 00:16.720
And we have learned there are two types of tables.

00:16.720 --> 00:19.320
We have permanent tables and temporary tables.

00:19.360 --> 00:23.480
Permanent tables lives in the database forever, as long as you don't drop them.

00:23.480 --> 00:27.440
But in the other hand, the temporary tables they have short lifetime.

00:27.440 --> 00:30.880
They will be dropped from the database once you end the session.

00:30.880 --> 00:35.760
Now we have learned as well there are two methods on how to create tables in databases.

00:35.760 --> 00:38.240
The first method is create inserts.

00:38.240 --> 00:40.040
This method involves two steps.

00:40.040 --> 00:46.520
The first one is defining and creating the table, and the second step is by inserting the data inside

00:46.520 --> 00:47.440
this new table.

00:47.440 --> 00:49.680
So you are creating something from the scratch.

00:49.680 --> 00:52.240
And the second method we call it CTAs.

00:52.400 --> 00:57.600
It's create as well brand new table but based on the result of a query.

00:57.600 --> 01:03.570
So this type is done with only one step, but it always needs another existing table and we have learned

01:03.570 --> 01:08.890
as well the difference between tables and views, where the main advantage of using tables created from

01:08.890 --> 01:16.290
cities is that to ensure the performance is fast enough at the end of the users or your reporting system.

01:16.290 --> 01:18.730
So we use CTAs instead of views.

01:19.010 --> 01:24.530
If the logic of the view is very complex and takes a lot of time to be executed in the database.

01:24.530 --> 01:30.770
And one more nice use case for the CTAs is that we can go and persist a snapshot of the data in order

01:30.770 --> 01:36.370
to analyze a bug and data quality issue, and to ensure that we have the exact data in order to find

01:36.410 --> 01:38.410
a solution for the bug and the issue.

01:38.450 --> 01:43.730
Now, we have learned as well that we can use temporary tables in order to store intermediate results

01:43.730 --> 01:49.610
in a temporary storage, and the main advantage of the temporary table is that the database automatically

01:49.610 --> 01:53.330
drops all the temporary tables when the session ends.

01:53.330 --> 01:58.810
And that's because for you, the intermediate results are not that important to live long time.
